{%- comment -%}
  tapi-cart-capture — tells the recovery service about an OTP verified cart.

  Renders no markup. Its only job is to hand assets/tapi-cart-capture.js an
  endpoint and an on/off switch.

  WHY IT EXISTS. Shopify files an abandoned checkout only once a shopper
  reaches its own contact step. COD King's OTP happens before that and writes
  _otpVerifiedPhoneNumber onto the CART, so everyone who verifies a number and
  leaves earlier is reachable but invisible to Shopify's abandoned list. The
  script posts those carts to the wa-automation service, which treats them as
  the primary source for cart recovery and keeps Shopify's list as a fallback.

  Nothing but a cart token, the already verified number and variant ids with
  quantities is sent. Every price the shopper is later offered against is read
  back from Shopify by the server, never taken from the browser.

  Clearing the endpoint switches the whole thing off, with no code change.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign s = section.settings
  assign on = false
  if s.enabled and s.endpoint != blank
    assign on = true
  endif
-%}

{%- if on -%}
  <script type="application/json" id="tapi-cart-capture-config">
    {
      "enabled": true,
      "endpoint": {{ s.endpoint | json }}
    }
  </script>
  <script src="{{ 'tapi-cart-capture.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Cart recovery capture",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "enabled",
      "label": "Enable cart recovery capture",
      "default": true,
      "info": "Lets WhatsApp cart recovery see carts that passed COD King's OTP but never reached Shopify checkout. Shopify's own abandoned checkout list misses those."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "endpoint",
      "label": "Capture endpoint",
      "default": "https://dqpboq7r05.execute-api.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/cart-capture",
      "info": "The wa-automation service's /cart-capture route. Leave blank to switch capture off entirely."
    }
  ],
  "presets": []
}
{% endschema %}
